-- title:
--   Proposition 6: the IFB iterates minimize $\Theta$; weak cluster points are minimizers
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a real Hilbert space, let Hypothesis H hold, and let $(u_k, y_k)$ be generated by (IFB). Then:
--
--   1. the values converge to the infimum,
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\Theta(u_k) = \inf_{x\in H}\Theta(x);$$
--   2. every weak sequential cluster point of $(u_k)$ lies in $\mathcal S = \operatorname{Argmin}\Theta$: if $u_{\varphi(k)} \rightharpoonup p$ along a strictly increasing $\varphi : \mathbb N\to\mathbb N$, then $p \in \mathcal S$;
--   3. if $\mathcal S = \emptyset$, then $\|u_k\| \to +\infty$.
--
--   The sequence is thus minimizing even when $\Theta$ has no minimizer.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\Theta(u_k)$ and $\inf\Theta$ are `EReal`-valued and the limit is taken in `EReal`. Weak convergence is tested against every $v \in H$ through inner products.
-- source:
--   Attouch, Peypouquet & Redont, A Dynamical Approach to an Inertial Forward-Backward Algorithm for Convex Minimization, authors' manuscript (Aug 2013) of SIAM J. Optim. (2014), DOI 10.1137/130910294, p. 9, Proposition 6

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_InertialFB_IFB_ConvexAnalysis
import Definitions.Def_InertialFB_IFB_Algorithm
import Definitions.Def_InertialFB_IFB_Lyapunov

open Filter Topology

namespace InertialFB.IFB

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]

/-- **Proposition 6** (Attouch–Peypouquet–Redont, p. 9). Under Hypothesis H, for every sequence
generated by (IFB): `Θ(u_k) → inf Θ`; every weak sequential cluster point of `(u_k)` lies in
`S = Argmin Θ`; and if `S = ∅` then `‖u_k‖ → +∞`. -/
theorem proposition6_minimizing (Φ : H → EReal) (Ψ : H → ℝ) (L a b lam : ℝ)
    (hH : HypothesisH Φ Ψ L a b lam) (u y : ℕ → H) (hIFB : IsIFBSeq Φ Ψ a b lam u y) :
    Tendsto (fun k => theta Φ Ψ (u k)) atTop (𝓝 (⨅ x, theta Φ Ψ x)) ∧
    (∀ p : H, (∃ φ : ℕ → ℕ, StrictMono φ ∧ WeakTendsto (u ∘ φ) p) → p ∈ argminSet Φ Ψ) ∧
    (argminSet Φ Ψ = ∅ → Tendsto (fun k => ‖u k‖) atTop atTop) := by sorry

end InertialFB.IFB
